{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792433715232,"sessionID":"ses_eaaa01f8affesgSTHulR12a46T","part":{"partID":"prt_1555ff612001XxUtpGUynBpBeR","sessionID":"ses_eaaa01f8affesgSTHulR12a46T","messageID":"msg_1555fee8c001Da40dZztCYLVH6","type":"tool","id":"call_01_q4xar8bgrrl4w8u6rymxrfia","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/application-atlas-production-pack/atlas/template-factory/jobs/job_7742b1c124be4c9ab3a0096da5cdd772/attempt-4/blueprint-code-0-1/source/RUNTIME_PROTOCOL.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/application-atlas-production-pack/atlas/template-factory/jobs/job_7742b1c124be4c9ab3a0096da5cdd772/attempt-4/blueprint-code-0-1/source/RUNTIME_PROTOCOL.md, lines 1-10\n1: Independent execution protocol requested: atlas.acceptance-runner.v1.\n2: Plan acceptance/runner.json LAST, alongside the actual programs and README. It must be exactly:\n3: {\"schema\":\"atlas.acceptance-runner.v1\",\"result_schema\":\"atlas.acceptance-result.v1\",\"cases\":{\"A01\":{\"args\":[\"--case\",\"{case_id}\",\"--base-url\",\"{base_url}\"]}}}.\n4: Include EVERY normative acceptance ID once. Each implementation is selected by Atlas from spec.acceptance, never overridden by the binding. Python .py and Node .js/.mjs/.cjs are supported; use only literals and {base_url}, {app_root}, {data_dir}, {case_id} placeholders. Bind each case to precise flags that its real program implements. CLI adapters use app_root (read-only application source); mutable fixtures go in data_dir. Web adapters use the exact base_url. External network is disabled; dependencies must already be supplied by the supported image or program, never assume Python in Node images or browser libraries are installed. Prefer standard-library checks when appropriate; unsupported browser prerequisites must report unavailable, never fake UI success.\n5: Every case invocation must perform real positive/negative behavior assertions and emit ONE JSON object to stdout (diagnostics on stderr). Keep the complete result within 64000 characters; truncated results cannot pass:\n6: {\"schema\":\"atlas.acceptance-result.v1\",\"case_id\":\"A01\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"assertions\":[{\"id\":\"behavior-1\",\"passed\":true,\"detail\":\"actual action and observation\"}]}.\n7: Return a nonempty set of genuine assertions, exit nonzero on failure, and use failed or unverified when appropriate. No unconditional pass, heading checks, fixture hardcodes, mocked target, --help-as-pass, or author execution claim. Unknown/missing case flags must fail explicitly. Factor shared setup while keeping per-case execution deterministic. Acceptance programs are frozen independently of the downstream application and must never import its own test verdict or modify the suite.\n8: README must document the target adapter, profile/runtime requirements, exact case flags, offline limitations, startup versus behavior evidence, and a root delivery.json example using schema atlas.application-delivery.v1, root '.' or 'app', exact source files and runtime {profile, install:[],build:[],start:[...],port:...} for web or {profile:'cli',install:[],build:[],smoke:[...]} for CLI. Uploaded metadata never supplies test commands. No application implementation is generated in this task.\n9: \n10: Host isolation contract: each acceptance program runs directly in an independent Python or Node image, e.g. `python /suite/acceptance/x.py`; its working directory is not guaranteed to be `/suite`, so imports must be based on the program location or another explicit path. `app_root` is the read-only application source. `data_dir` is only the tester's mutable scratch directory at `/state`, never the application's database. The application and tester share only network access. Supported delivery profiles are exactly `python-web`, `node-web`, `static-web`, and `cli`; `web` is invalid. A web acceptance program must exercise the supplied `base_url`. Start commands are literal argv arrays: placeholders such as `{port}` or `{data_dir}` are not interpolated inside an argument. A process-restart acceptance claim needs a concrete adapter contract for launching the same frozen application from `app_root` as a dedicated process, with isolated per-instance scratch, doing real app actions, stopping that process, starting it again, and observing persisted app behavior. A new HTTP client or a database created by the tester does not prove app restart or persistence. A read-only external target that cannot be restarted requires separate external verification and must remain explicitly unverified for restart behavior; never claim a pass for it.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/application-atlas-production-pack/atlas/template-factory/jobs/job_7742b1c124be4c9ab3a0096da5cdd772/attempt-4/blueprint-code-0-1/source/RUNTIME_PROTOCOL.md, lines 1-10\n1: Independent execution protocol requested: atlas.acceptance-runner.v1.\n2: Plan acceptance/runner.json LAST, alongside the actual programs and README. It must be exactly:\n3: {\"schema\":\"atlas.acceptance-runner.v1\",\"result_schema\":\"atlas.acceptance-result.v1\",\"cases\":{\"A01\":{\"args\":[\"--case\",\"{case_id}\",\"--base-url\",\"{base_url}\"]}}}.\n4: Include EVERY normative acceptance ID once. Each implementation is selected by Atlas from spec.acceptance, never overridden by the binding. Python .py and Node .js/.mjs/.cjs are supported; use only literals and {base_url}, {app_root}, {data_dir}, {case_id} placeholders. Bind each case to precise flags that its real program implements. CLI adapters use app_root (read-only application source); mutable fixtures go in data_dir. Web adapters use the exact base_url. External network is disabled; dependencies must already be supplied by the supported image or program, never assume Python in Node images or browser libraries are installed. Prefer standard-library checks when appropriate; unsupported browser prerequisites must report unavailable, never fake UI success.\n5: Every case invocation must perform real positive/negative behavior assertions and emit ONE JSON object to stdout (diagnostics on stderr). Keep the complete result within 64000 characters; truncated results cannot pass:\n6: {\"schema\":\"atlas.acceptance-result.v1\",\"case_id\":\"A01\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"assertions\":[{\"id\":\"behavior-1\",\"passed\":true,\"detail\":\"actual action and observation\"}]}.\n7: Return a nonempty set of genuine assertions, exit nonzero on failure, and use failed or unverified when appropriate. No unconditional pass, heading checks, fixture hardcodes, mocked target, --help-as-pass, or author execution claim. Unknown/missing case flags must fail explicitly. Factor shared setup while keeping per-case execution deterministic. Acceptance programs are frozen independently of the downstream application and must never import its own test verdict or modify the suite.\n8: README must document the target adapter, profile/runtime requirements, exact case flags, offline limitations, startup versus behavior evidence, and a root delivery.json example using schema atlas.application-delivery.v1, root '.' or 'app', exact source files and runtime {profile, install:[],build:[],start:[...],port:...} for web or {profile:'cli',install:[],build:[],smoke:[...]} for CLI. Uploaded metadata never supplies test commands. No application implementation is generated in this task.\n9: \n10: Host isolation contract: each acceptance program runs directly in an independent Python or Node image, e.g. `python /suite/acceptance/x.py`; its working directory is not guaranteed to be `/suite`, so imports must be based on the program location or another explicit path. `app_root` is the read-only application source. `data_dir` is only the tester's mutable scratch directory at `/state`, never the application's database. The application and tester share only network access. Supported delivery profiles are exactly `python-web`, `node-web`, `static-web`, and `cli`; `web` is invalid. A web acceptance program must exercise the supplied `base_url`. Start commands are literal argv arrays: placeholders such as `{port}` or `{data_dir}` are not interpolated inside an argument. A process-restart acceptance claim needs a concrete adapter contract for launching the same frozen application from `app_root` as a dedicated process, with isolated per-instance scratch, doing real app actions, stopping that process, starting it again, and observing persisted app behavior. A new HTTP client or a database created by the tester does not prove app restart or persistence. A read-only external target that cannot be restarted requires separate external verification and must remain explicitly unverified for restart behavior; never claim a pass for it."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/application-atlas-production-pack/atlas/template-factory/jobs/job_7742b1c124be4c9ab3a0096da5cdd772/attempt-4/blueprint-code-0-1/source/RUNTIME_PROTOCOL.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1792433714706,"end":1792433715232}}}}
