{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792433729716,"sessionID":"ses_eaaa01f8affesgSTHulR12a46T","part":{"partID":"prt_15560307d001igtoWBHZ5zyUDi","sessionID":"ses_eaaa01f8affesgSTHulR12a46T","messageID":"msg_155601da1001ZfgmdhSJSN3e4A","type":"tool","id":"call_00_fewkxcyynhg9z3usef8dqva3","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/application-atlas-production-pack/atlas/template-factory/jobs/job_7742b1c124be4c9ab3a0096da5cdd772/attempt-4/blueprint-code-0-1/source/FORMAT.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/application-atlas-production-pack/atlas/template-factory/jobs/job_7742b1c124be4c9ab3a0096da5cdd772/attempt-4/blueprint-code-0-1/source/FORMAT.md, lines 1-24\n1: Produce a cognitive product blueprint for the PINNED leaf/scenario using supplied research, not a complete application. Read input.json, source/RESEARCH.md and source/FORMAT.md completely.\n2: Return {\"spec\":{\"title\":\"...\",\"roles\":[{\"id\":\"R01\",\"name\":\"...\",\"responsibility\":\"...\"}],\"features\":[{\"id\":\"F01\",\"name\":\"...\",\"phase\":\"P0 or null\",\"applicability\":\"current required / later / not applicable / decision needed\",\"reason\":\"...\",\"sources\":[\"S01\"],\"acceptance\":[\"A01\"]}],\"decisions\":[{\"id\":\"D01\",\"question\":\"...\",\"default\":\"recommended reversible default and reason\",\"when_to_ask\":\"actual decision trigger, not every engineering choice\",\"impact\":\"...\",\"status\":\"...\"}],\"phases\":[{\"id\":\"P0\",\"title\":\"...\",\"goal\":\"user capability\",\"features\":[\"F01\"],\"acceptance\":[\"A01\"],\"status\":\"not implemented\"}],\"acceptance\":[{\"id\":\"A01\",\"phase\":\"P0\",\"goal\":\"observable behavior\",\"type\":\"positive|negative\",\"features\":[\"F01\"],\"implementation\":\"acceptance/run.cjs\",\"status\":\"not_run\"}],\"architecture_markdown\":\"default stack with reasons and alternatives, data model, API/error/state contracts, UI/CLI adapter contract for tests, nonfunctional requirements, limits\",\"limits\":[\"...\"],\"contract_coverage\":{\"schema\":\"atlas.contract-coverage.v1\",\"review_rules_version\":\"atlas.current-required-contract.v1\",\"features\":[{\"feature_id\":\"F01\",\"design_basis\":\"scenario or justified product commitment\",\"entry\":\"reachable page/form or supporting journey\",\"action\":\"user action and fields\",\"success_state\":\"persisted or observable result\",\"navigation\":\"success navigation or explicit none and why\",\"failure\":\"user-visible failure\",\"recovery\":\"available recovery action\",\"acceptance_ids\":[\"A01\"]}] }},\"file_plan\":[{\"path\":\"acceptance/common.cjs\",\"purpose\":\"shared request/assertion helper; exact exports and adapter interfaces\"},{\"path\":\"acceptance/p0.cjs\",\"purpose\":\"P0 real target cases; list IDs and behavior\"},{\"path\":\"acceptance/README.md\",\"purpose\":\"complete setup/run instructions\"}]}. Return a SPECIFICATION AND FILE PLAN ONLY, never file contents in this stage. Use a small coherent set of programs split by phase; shared helpers first, phase tests next, dependency manifests and README last. Each file must f... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n3: Atlas supplies id, kind, schema, version, confirmed scenario, sources, evidence and all main Markdown documents. Avoid embedding the candidate version in title; Atlas displays version separately. Do NOT return or replace those reserved fields/documents, the integrity file, plan.json or agent configs. Match the supplied schema and source IDs; maintain bidirectional feature-phase-case references. Use review rules \"atlas.current-required-contract.v1\" for generation and review. Include spec.contract_coverage inside spec using {\"schema\":\"atlas.contract-coverage.v1\",\"review_rules_version\":\"atlas.current-required-contract.v1\",\"features\":[{\"feature_id\":\"F01\",\"design_basis\":\"scenario or justified product commitment\",\"entry\":\"reachable page/form or supporting journey\",\"action\":\"user action and fields\",\"success_state\":\"persisted or observable result\",\"navigation\":\"success navigation or explicit none and why\",\"failure\":\"user-visible failure\",\"recovery\":\"available recovery action\",\"acceptance_ids\":[\"A01\"]}]}; provide one row for each current-required P0 feature and use only exact existing IDs. This mapping is structurally checked, while independent semantic review judges whether the route and behavior actually work. Phases are ordered by delivery. The FIRST phase must deliver the complete core journey already promised by the confirmed scenario (entry, primary actions, useful result, persistence when relevant, failure and recovery). Do not split indispensable confirmed steps across later phases merely to make P0 small; later phases add mature or optional capabilities. Preserve mature category knowledge and applicability without requiring all of it upfront. For a revision whose fixed IDs prevent coherent rephasing, report that conflict rather than silently dropping scope. A feature phase is its introduction phase: it needs a test in that phase, and later cases may regress it; earlier cases must never depend on future capabilities. Every phased capability needs acceptance; non-appl... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n4: Acceptance programs must operate on a REAL target supplied by URL/CLI parameter, include behavior assertions and high-risk negative cases for each phase, exit nonzero on failed assertions, and expose precise setup plus adapter contracts. Never substitute file/heading presence or mock responses for user behavior. If tests accept authentication parameters, keep credentials restricted to the explicitly configured target; never attach global headers to external navigation/fixtures or log secret values. Unsupported authentication modes must fail explicitly as infrastructure/incomplete, not silently skip or pass. Do not implement the downstream app or pretend tests ran. No empty programs, placeholders, encoded archives, credential files, upstream code or hidden model calls. Code must be newly authored, except small Atlas references explicitly provided. Do not run it; Atlas will record programs as present but NOT executed. Authored prose follows input.language. When input.guidance_file or input.design_feedback_file is supplied, read that full file. Trace every current user-facing capability through its declared UI, CLI or API entry, action, success, error and recovery. API-only products do not need an invented UI; an API alone is insufficient for a declared human UI capability. When a versioned REPAIR_SCOPE.json is supplied, treat it as binding: edit only listed authored field paths and program files, preserve all feature IDs, phases, current-required statuses and other authored fields; keep every existing assertion intent except changes explicitly authorized in the supplied scope. The host rejects out-of-scope diffs before freeze. When revision is supplied, read source/REVISION.md and source/REVIEWS.md completely; long JSON instruction strings may be truncated by the tool. Read prior implementation/failure_evidence only if supplied; fix actual contradictions while keeping the confirmed scenario fixed.\n5: For current-required human-interface capabilities, specify the real user entry, submitted fields, success navigation, visible error and recovery path. Acceptance should exercise the declared interface and keep any supporting API assertions distinct from user-interface behavior. For HTML errors, preserve submitted values or expose a runnable recovery control, and leave storage unchanged on failure. Do not create a new user-interface feature without a matching feature ID and acceptance. For the independent browser contract, use stable selectors and named fields that match the authored interface, and verify actual navigation targets without fetching external targets.\n6: Host-owned policy for this exact scenario/product identity:\n7: - revision: CP-1\n8: - category_contract: {\"bookmark_move\": {\"acceptance_id\": \"A12\", \"html_failure\": \"Show form-error, retain submitted values, and make no writes.\", \"html_field\": \"category_id\", \"html_semantics\": \"Resolve the submitted ID to an existing category name.\", \"invalid_html_values\": [\"omitted\", \"empty\", \"unknown_id\"], \"invalid_json_values\": [\"omitted\", \"JSON null\", \"empty\", \"whitespace_only\", \"121_characters\"], \"invalid_result\": {\"code\": \"invalid_category\", \"status\": 400}, \"json_field\": \"category\", \"json_semantics\": \"Category NAME, never category ID.\", \"never_create_from_html_id\": true, \"valid_new_json_name\": \"Automatically create and use the named category.\"}, \"bookmark_save\": {\"acceptance_id\": \"A12\", \"field_semantics\": \"Category NAME, never category ID.\", \"html_failure\": \"Show form-error, retain submitted values, and make no writes.\", \"html_field\": \"category\", \"html_null\": \"HTML forms have no native null value.\", \"invalid_result\": {\"code\": \"invalid_category\", \"status\": 400}, \"invalid_values\": [\"empty\", \"whitespace_only\", \"121_characters\"], \"json_field\": \"category\", \"omitted_or_null_json\": \"Use the default category.\", \"valid_new_name\": \"Automatically create and use the named category.\"}, \"management\": {\"acceptance_id\": \"A04\", \"existing_category_identity_field\": \"category_id\", \"html_failure\": \"Show form-error, retain submitted values, and make no writes.\", \"html_invalid_values\": [\"omitted\", \"empty\", \"whitespace_only\", \"121_characters\"], \"input_field\": \"name\", \"invalid_result\": {\"code\": \"invalid_name\", \"status\": 400}, \"json_failure\": \"Return invalid_name and make no writes.\", \"json_invalid_values\": [\"omitted\", \"empty\", \"whitespace_only\", \"121_characters\", \"null\"], \"operations\": [\"category_create\", \"category_rename\"]}, \"unknown_get_filter\": \"Return an empty result; do not treat an unknown category filter as an error.\"}\n9: - search_contract: Search is a case-insensitive substring over title, hostname, and description, with optional category filtering applied together. Search does not match tags or raw URL substrings.\n10: - url_policy: {\"absolute\": true, \"dns_required\": false, \"nonempty_valid_hostname\": true, \"p0_fetch\": false, \"preserve_original_text\": true, \"schemes\": [\"http\", \"https\"], \"single_label_hosts\": true}\n11: - authorized_assertion_adaptation: A02 may replace only its single-label-hostname rejection example with a positive example; missing scheme, unsupported scheme, empty hostname, and invalid hostname must remain rejected without writing.\n12: - adaptation: The source IndexedDB/Dexie and SPA are source facts. Adapt persistence and rendering to the declared target profile; do not turn source facts into target requirements. Preserve the exact A04 category-management and A12 bookmark save/move contracts above, plus the title/hostname/description search contract.\n13: Independent execution protocol requested: atlas.acceptance-runner.v1.\n14: Plan acceptance/runner.json LAST, alongside the actual programs and README. It must be exactly:\n15: {\"schema\":\"atlas.acceptance-runner.v1\",\"result_schema\":\"atlas.acceptance-result.v1\",\"cases\":{\"A01\":{\"args\":[\"--case\",\"{case_id}\",\"--base-url\",\"{base_url}\"]}}}.\n16: Include EVERY normative acceptance ID once. Each implementation is selected by Atlas from spec.acceptance, never overridden by the binding. Python .py and Node .js/.mjs/.cjs are supported; use only literals and {base_url}, {app_root}, {data_dir}, {case_id} placeholders. Bind each case to precise flags that its real program implements. CLI adapters use app_root (read-only application source); mutable fixtures go in data_dir. Web adapters use the exact base_url. External network is disabled; dependencies must already be supplied by the supported image or program, never assume Python in Node images or browser libraries are installed. Prefer standard-library checks when appropriate; unsupported browser prerequisites must report unavailable, never fake UI success.\n17: Every case invocation must perform real positive/negative behavior assertions and emit ONE JSON object to stdout (diagnostics on stderr). Keep the complete result within 64000 characters; truncated results cannot pass:\n18: {\"schema\":\"atlas.acceptance-result.v1\",\"case_id\":\"A01\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"assertions\":[{\"id\":\"behavior-1\",\"passed\":true,\"detail\":\"actual action and observation\"}]}.\n19: Return a nonempty set of genuine assertions, exit nonzero on failure, and use failed or unverified when appropriate. No unconditional pass, heading checks, fixture hardcodes, mocked target, --help-as-pass, or author execution claim. Unknown/missing case flags must fail explicitly. Factor shared setup while keeping per-case execution deterministic. Acceptance programs are frozen independently of the downstream application and must never import its own test verdict or modify the suite.\n20: README must document the target adapter, profile/runtime requirements, exact case flags, offline limitations, startup versus behavior evidence, and a root delivery.json example using schema atlas.application-delivery.v1, root '.' or 'app', exact source files and runtime {profile, install:[],build:[],start:[...],port:...} for web or {profile:'cli',install:[],build:[],smoke:[...]} for CLI. Uploaded metadata never supplies test commands. No application implementation is generated in this task.\n21: \n22: Host isolation contract: each acceptance program runs directly in an independent Python or Node image, e.g. `python /suite/acceptance/x.py`; its working directory is not guaranteed to be `/suite`, so imports must be based on the program location or another explicit path. `app_root` is the read-only application source. `data_dir` is only the tester's mutable scratch directory at `/state`, never the application's database. The application and tester share only network access. Supported delivery profiles are exactly `python-web`, `node-web`, `static-web`, and `cli`; `web` is invalid. A web acceptance program must exercise the supplied `base_url`. Start commands are literal argv arrays: placeholders such as `{port}` or `{data_dir}` are not interpolated inside an argument. A process-restart acceptance claim needs a concrete adapter contract for launching the same frozen application from `app_root` as a dedicated process, with isolated per-instance scratch, doing real app actions, stopping that process, starting it again, and observing persisted app behavior. A new HTTP client or a database created by the tester does not prove app restart or persistence. A read-only external target that cannot be restarted requires separate external verification and must remain explicitly unverified for restart behavior; never claim a pass for it.\n23: \n24: V1: Read CASE_BASIS.json, ACCEPTED_CASE_FACTS.json, and CASE_DESIGN.json. Host-owned fixed case/evidence IDs are immutable; use research source IDs in features. Distinguish borrowed behavior, adaptations and new designs in architecture and reasons. V1 downstream profile is python-web on Python3.12 with standard library/SQLite; acceptance must use Python standard library, not npm/Playwright dependencies. Real UI journey will also be checked by an independent executor outside the suite. Do not invent runtime results. Keep P0 complete and executable offline. Cases and source have already been researched; do not search again.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/application-atlas-production-pack/atlas/template-factory/jobs/job_7742b1c124be4c9ab3a0096da5cdd772/attempt-4/blueprint-code-0-1/source/FORMAT.md, lines 1-24\n1: Produce a cognitive product blueprint for the PINNED leaf/scenario using supplied research, not a complete application. Read input.json, source/RESEARCH.md and source/FORMAT.md completely.\n2: Return {\"spec\":{\"title\":\"...\",\"roles\":[{\"id\":\"R01\",\"name\":\"...\",\"responsibility\":\"...\"}],\"features\":[{\"id\":\"F01\",\"name\":\"...\",\"phase\":\"P0 or null\",\"applicability\":\"current required / later / not applicable / decision needed\",\"reason\":\"...\",\"sources\":[\"S01\"],\"acceptance\":[\"A01\"]}],\"decisions\":[{\"id\":\"D01\",\"question\":\"...\",\"default\":\"recommended reversible default and reason\",\"when_to_ask\":\"actual decision trigger, not every engineering choice\",\"impact\":\"...\",\"status\":\"...\"}],\"phases\":[{\"id\":\"P0\",\"title\":\"...\",\"goal\":\"user capability\",\"features\":[\"F01\"],\"acceptance\":[\"A01\"],\"status\":\"not implemented\"}],\"acceptance\":[{\"id\":\"A01\",\"phase\":\"P0\",\"goal\":\"observable behavior\",\"type\":\"positive|negative\",\"features\":[\"F01\"],\"implementation\":\"acceptance/run.cjs\",\"status\":\"not_run\"}],\"architecture_markdown\":\"default stack with reasons and alternatives, data model, API/error/state contracts, UI/CLI adapter contract for tests, nonfunctional requirements, limits\",\"limits\":[\"...\"],\"contract_coverage\":{\"schema\":\"atlas.contract-coverage.v1\",\"review_rules_version\":\"atlas.current-required-contract.v1\",\"features\":[{\"feature_id\":\"F01\",\"design_basis\":\"scenario or justified product commitment\",\"entry\":\"reachable page/form or supporting journey\",\"action\":\"user action and fields\",\"success_state\":\"persisted or observable result\",\"navigation\":\"success navigation or explicit none and why\",\"failure\":\"user-visible failure\",\"recovery\":\"available recovery action\",\"acceptance_ids\":[\"A01\"]}] }},\"file_plan\":[{\"path\":\"acceptance/common.cjs\",\"purpose\":\"shared request/assertion helper; exact exports and adapter interfaces\"},{\"path\":\"acceptance/p0.cjs\",\"purpose\":\"P0 real target cases; list IDs and behavior\"},{\"path\":\"acceptance/README.md\",\"purpose\":\"complete setup/run instructions\"}]}. Return a SPECIFICATION AND FILE PLAN ONLY, never file contents in this stage. Use a small coherent set of programs split by phase; shared helpers first, phase tests next, dependency manifests and README last. Each file must f... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n3: Atlas supplies id, kind, schema, version, confirmed scenario, sources, evidence and all main Markdown documents. Avoid embedding the candidate version in title; Atlas displays version separately. Do NOT return or replace those reserved fields/documents, the integrity file, plan.json or agent configs. Match the supplied schema and source IDs; maintain bidirectional feature-phase-case references. Use review rules \"atlas.current-required-contract.v1\" for generation and review. Include spec.contract_coverage inside spec using {\"schema\":\"atlas.contract-coverage.v1\",\"review_rules_version\":\"atlas.current-required-contract.v1\",\"features\":[{\"feature_id\":\"F01\",\"design_basis\":\"scenario or justified product commitment\",\"entry\":\"reachable page/form or supporting journey\",\"action\":\"user action and fields\",\"success_state\":\"persisted or observable result\",\"navigation\":\"success navigation or explicit none and why\",\"failure\":\"user-visible failure\",\"recovery\":\"available recovery action\",\"acceptance_ids\":[\"A01\"]}]}; provide one row for each current-required P0 feature and use only exact existing IDs. This mapping is structurally checked, while independent semantic review judges whether the route and behavior actually work. Phases are ordered by delivery. The FIRST phase must deliver the complete core journey already promised by the confirmed scenario (entry, primary actions, useful result, persistence when relevant, failure and recovery). Do not split indispensable confirmed steps across later phases merely to make P0 small; later phases add mature or optional capabilities. Preserve mature category knowledge and applicability without requiring all of it upfront. For a revision whose fixed IDs prevent coherent rephasing, report that conflict rather than silently dropping scope. A feature phase is its introduction phase: it needs a test in that phase, and later cases may regress it; earlier cases must never depend on future capabilities. Every phased capability needs acceptance; non-appl... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n4: Acceptance programs must operate on a REAL target supplied by URL/CLI parameter, include behavior assertions and high-risk negative cases for each phase, exit nonzero on failed assertions, and expose precise setup plus adapter contracts. Never substitute file/heading presence or mock responses for user behavior. If tests accept authentication parameters, keep credentials restricted to the explicitly configured target; never attach global headers to external navigation/fixtures or log secret values. Unsupported authentication modes must fail explicitly as infrastructure/incomplete, not silently skip or pass. Do not implement the downstream app or pretend tests ran. No empty programs, placeholders, encoded archives, credential files, upstream code or hidden model calls. Code must be newly authored, except small Atlas references explicitly provided. Do not run it; Atlas will record programs as present but NOT executed. Authored prose follows input.language. When input.guidance_file or input.design_feedback_file is supplied, read that full file. Trace every current user-facing capability through its declared UI, CLI or API entry, action, success, error and recovery. API-only products do not need an invented UI; an API alone is insufficient for a declared human UI capability. When a versioned REPAIR_SCOPE.json is supplied, treat it as binding: edit only listed authored field paths and program files, preserve all feature IDs, phases, current-required statuses and other authored fields; keep every existing assertion intent except changes explicitly authorized in the supplied scope. The host rejects out-of-scope diffs before freeze. When revision is supplied, read source/REVISION.md and source/REVIEWS.md completely; long JSON instruction strings may be truncated by the tool. Read prior implementation/failure_evidence only if supplied; fix actual contradictions while keeping the confirmed scenario fixed.\n5: For current-required human-interface capabilities, specify the real user entry, submitted fields, success navigation, visible error and recovery path. Acceptance should exercise the declared interface and keep any supporting API assertions distinct from user-interface behavior. For HTML errors, preserve submitted values or expose a runnable recovery control, and leave storage unchanged on failure. Do not create a new user-interface feature without a matching feature ID and acceptance. For the independent browser contract, use stable selectors and named fields that match the authored interface, and verify actual navigation targets without fetching external targets.\n6: Host-owned policy for this exact scenario/product identity:\n7: - revision: CP-1\n8: - category_contract: {\"bookmark_move\": {\"acceptance_id\": \"A12\", \"html_failure\": \"Show form-error, retain submitted values, and make no writes.\", \"html_field\": \"category_id\", \"html_semantics\": \"Resolve the submitted ID to an existing category name.\", \"invalid_html_values\": [\"omitted\", \"empty\", \"unknown_id\"], \"invalid_json_values\": [\"omitted\", \"JSON null\", \"empty\", \"whitespace_only\", \"121_characters\"], \"invalid_result\": {\"code\": \"invalid_category\", \"status\": 400}, \"json_field\": \"category\", \"json_semantics\": \"Category NAME, never category ID.\", \"never_create_from_html_id\": true, \"valid_new_json_name\": \"Automatically create and use the named category.\"}, \"bookmark_save\": {\"acceptance_id\": \"A12\", \"field_semantics\": \"Category NAME, never category ID.\", \"html_failure\": \"Show form-error, retain submitted values, and make no writes.\", \"html_field\": \"category\", \"html_null\": \"HTML forms have no native null value.\", \"invalid_result\": {\"code\": \"invalid_category\", \"status\": 400}, \"invalid_values\": [\"empty\", \"whitespace_only\", \"121_characters\"], \"json_field\": \"category\", \"omitted_or_null_json\": \"Use the default category.\", \"valid_new_name\": \"Automatically create and use the named category.\"}, \"management\": {\"acceptance_id\": \"A04\", \"existing_category_identity_field\": \"category_id\", \"html_failure\": \"Show form-error, retain submitted values, and make no writes.\", \"html_invalid_values\": [\"omitted\", \"empty\", \"whitespace_only\", \"121_characters\"], \"input_field\": \"name\", \"invalid_result\": {\"code\": \"invalid_name\", \"status\": 400}, \"json_failure\": \"Return invalid_name and make no writes.\", \"json_invalid_values\": [\"omitted\", \"empty\", \"whitespace_only\", \"121_characters\", \"null\"], \"operations\": [\"category_create\", \"category_rename\"]}, \"unknown_get_filter\": \"Return an empty result; do not treat an unknown category filter as an error.\"}\n9: - search_contract: Search is a case-insensitive substring over title, hostname, and description, with optional category filtering applied together. Search does not match tags or raw URL substrings.\n10: - url_policy: {\"absolute\": true, \"dns_required\": false, \"nonempty_valid_hostname\": true, \"p0_fetch\": false, \"preserve_original_text\": true, \"schemes\": [\"http\", \"https\"], \"single_label_hosts\": true}\n11: - authorized_assertion_adaptation: A02 may replace only its single-label-hostname rejection example with a positive example; missing scheme, unsupported scheme, empty hostname, and invalid hostname must remain rejected without writing.\n12: - adaptation: The source IndexedDB/Dexie and SPA are source facts. Adapt persistence and rendering to the declared target profile; do not turn source facts into target requirements. Preserve the exact A04 category-management and A12 bookmark save/move contracts above, plus the title/hostname/description search contract.\n13: Independent execution protocol requested: atlas.acceptance-runner.v1.\n14: Plan acceptance/runner.json LAST, alongside the actual programs and README. It must be exactly:\n15: {\"schema\":\"atlas.acceptance-runner.v1\",\"result_schema\":\"atlas.acceptance-result.v1\",\"cases\":{\"A01\":{\"args\":[\"--case\",\"{case_id}\",\"--base-url\",\"{base_url}\"]}}}.\n16: Include EVERY normative acceptance ID once. Each implementation is selected by Atlas from spec.acceptance, never overridden by the binding. Python .py and Node .js/.mjs/.cjs are supported; use only literals and {base_url}, {app_root}, {data_dir}, {case_id} placeholders. Bind each case to precise flags that its real program implements. CLI adapters use app_root (read-only application source); mutable fixtures go in data_dir. Web adapters use the exact base_url. External network is disabled; dependencies must already be supplied by the supported image or program, never assume Python in Node images or browser libraries are installed. Prefer standard-library checks when appropriate; unsupported browser prerequisites must report unavailable, never fake UI success.\n17: Every case invocation must perform real positive/negative behavior assertions and emit ONE JSON object to stdout (diagnostics on stderr). Keep the complete result within 64000 characters; truncated results cannot pass:\n18: {\"schema\":\"atlas.acceptance-result.v1\",\"case_id\":\"A01\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"assertions\":[{\"id\":\"behavior-1\",\"passed\":true,\"detail\":\"actual action and observation\"}]}.\n19: Return a nonempty set of genuine assertions, exit nonzero on failure, and use failed or unverified when appropriate. No unconditional pass, heading checks, fixture hardcodes, mocked target, --help-as-pass, or author execution claim. Unknown/missing case flags must fail explicitly. Factor shared setup while keeping per-case execution deterministic. Acceptance programs are frozen independently of the downstream application and must never import its own test verdict or modify the suite.\n20: README must document the target adapter, profile/runtime requirements, exact case flags, offline limitations, startup versus behavior evidence, and a root delivery.json example using schema atlas.application-delivery.v1, root '.' or 'app', exact source files and runtime {profile, install:[],build:[],start:[...],port:...} for web or {profile:'cli',install:[],build:[],smoke:[...]} for CLI. Uploaded metadata never supplies test commands. No application implementation is generated in this task.\n21: \n22: Host isolation contract: each acceptance program runs directly in an independent Python or Node image, e.g. `python /suite/acceptance/x.py`; its working directory is not guaranteed to be `/suite`, so imports must be based on the program location or another explicit path. `app_root` is the read-only application source. `data_dir` is only the tester's mutable scratch directory at `/state`, never the application's database. The application and tester share only network access. Supported delivery profiles are exactly `python-web`, `node-web`, `static-web`, and `cli`; `web` is invalid. A web acceptance program must exercise the supplied `base_url`. Start commands are literal argv arrays: placeholders such as `{port}` or `{data_dir}` are not interpolated inside an argument. A process-restart acceptance claim needs a concrete adapter contract for launching the same frozen application from `app_root` as a dedicated process, with isolated per-instance scratch, doing real app actions, stopping that process, starting it again, and observing persisted app behavior. A new HTTP client or a database created by the tester does not prove app restart or persistence. A read-only external target that cannot be restarted requires separate external verification and must remain explicitly unverified for restart behavior; never claim a pass for it.\n23: \n24: V1: Read CASE_BASIS.json, ACCEPTED_CASE_FACTS.json, and CASE_DESIGN.json. Host-owned fixed case/evidence IDs are immutable; use research source IDs in features. Distinguish borrowed behavior, adaptations and new designs in architecture and reasons. V1 downstream profile is python-web on Python3.12 with standard library/SQLite; acceptance must use Python standard library, not npm/Playwright dependencies. Real UI journey will also be checked by an independent executor outside the suite. Do not invent runtime results. Keep P0 complete and executable offline. Cases and source have already been researched; do not search again."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/application-atlas-production-pack/atlas/template-factory/jobs/job_7742b1c124be4c9ab3a0096da5cdd772/attempt-4/blueprint-code-0-1/source/FORMAT.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1792433729661,"end":1792433729716}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792433729717,"sessionID":"ses_eaaa01f8affesgSTHulR12a46T","part":{"partID":"prt_1556030a7001ebjLk0LVC1ckmu","sessionID":"ses_eaaa01f8affesgSTHulR12a46T","messageID":"msg_155601da1001ZfgmdhSJSN3e4A","type":"tool","id":"call_01_ozc6jwaxugr7fz35ngddm5vb","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/application-atlas-production-pack/atlas/template-factory/jobs/job_7742b1c124be4c9ab3a0096da5cdd772/attempt-4/blueprint-code-0-1/source/CASE_DESIGN.json"},"output":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/application-atlas-production-pack/atlas/template-factory/jobs/job_7742b1c124be4c9ab3a0096da5cdd772/attempt-4/blueprint-code-0-1/source/CASE_DESIGN.json, lines 1-93\n1: [\n2:  {\n3:   \"capability\": \"F08: a single-user personal library persisted in SQLite that survives browser sessions and server restarts, with records queried from the database for every request rather than held in a browser store.\",\n4:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n5:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n6:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_35e41aab676021eb\",\n7:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_86ed2327f33a3ca8\",\n8:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_922f1dbc84912d99\",\n9:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_e7dd8d32c05c39f9\"\n10:   ],\n11:   \"reason\": \"The evidence shows Dexie writes on save/delete and a one-time db.bookmarks.toArray() hydration into an in-memory RippleMap, scoped to one browser profile with no sync. The target adopts local, single-user, cross-session retention but replaces IndexedDB/Dexie and in-memory hydration with SQLite on the Python server; it does not claim browser-profile persistence, multi-device sync, or the source map as target design.\"\n12:  },\n13:  {\n14:   \"capability\": \"F11: the library is delivered as server-rendered HTML pages and forms with POST/redirect/GET for add, edit and organize actions, including a ready empty-library view.\",\n15:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n16:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n17:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_06c81a165e03c96a\",\n18:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_86ed2327f33a3ca8\",\n19:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_e7dd8d32c05c39f9\"\n20:   ],\n21:   \"reason\": \"The evidence describes a client-mounted SPA: Edit is an in-page dialog populated from item fields, and component creation loads Dexie rows into a client RippleMap. The target renders lists, forms and empty state as Python 3.12 HTML responses, so the SPA mount, client-side dialog state and Dexie hydration are not carried over; only the save-now/find-later user loop is retained.\"\n22:  },\n23:  {\n24:   \"capability\": \"A deliberate save creates a URL-anchored record with a stable id, derived hostname, createdAt and initial state, and later edits preserve the record identity and creation/visit fields.\",\n25:   \"disposition\": \"adopted\",\n26:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n27:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_05babdea64ba9858\"\n28:   ],\n29:   \"reason\": \"Evidence defines bm-prefixed UUID identity, hostname derivation, createdAt and default state, and preserves id/createdAt/visit fields on edit. The target adopts this record lifecycle as a user-facing capability, with SQLite providing durability; the source's free-text tag constraints are treated separately in the category decision, not silently imported as target rules.\"\n30:  },\n31:  {\n32:   \"capability\": \"URL validation accepts only absolute, parseable HTTP(S) URLs with a nonempty valid hostname, allows single-label hosts such as http://localhost, preserves the original URL text, and rejects malformed, non-HTTP(S) or empty-host input without writing; no DNS or online-reachability check is performed.\",\n33:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n34:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n35:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_1596da4a90687ca5\"\n36:   ],\n37:   \"reason\": \"The upstream Valibot rule is a dotted-host regex that requires a dot-separated domain and an alphabetic top-level suffix, so it rejects localhost. That regex is retained as a source fact and mapped as adjusted, not reused as the target rule: the target parses the URL, checks the http/https scheme, absolute form and hostname presence, permits single-label hosts, and stores the entered string unchanged.\"\n38:  },\n39:  {\n40:   \"capability\": \"Create, rename and delete named categories with validation and with protection or reassignment when a category still contains records, assign one at save time, move records between categories, and default uncategorized saves into an Inbox category.\",\n41:   \"disposition\": \"new_design\",\n42:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n43:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_3168bcd465b6a043\",\n44:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_6bbd7a588896fe31\"\n45:   ],\n46:   \"reason\": \"Evidence shows the source has no category entity: classification is only up to five free-text tags, there is no collection CRUD or separate move, and the form rejects saves with zero tags. The target therefore designs first-class categories, an inbox default for unclassified capture and an explicit move action; these are new target concepts, not source-derived tag behavior.\"\n47:  },\n48:  {\n49:   \"capability\": \"Browse one category and see only its active records, with a category count that agrees with the listed records after adds, moves and restores.\",\n50:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n51:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n52:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_c4ad7e52e5713628\",\n53:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_9ab6b0e51811a16d\"\n54:   ],\n55:   \"reason\": \"Source facts derive tag counts by scanning all in-memory bookmarks and filter records by requiring every selected tag. The target computes category counts and category-scoped lists in SQL over active, non-deleted rows so the count and the list stay consistent; the source tag-sidebar algorithm is not the target implementation.\"\n56:  },\n57:  {\n58:   \"capability\": \"Search the selected category by keyword across title, hostname and description using case-insensitive substring matching, retaining category and query and rendering matching or explicit empty results.\",\n59:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n60:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n61:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_9ab6b0e51811a16d\",\n62:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_e62ae7e0a2c68ba1\"\n63:   ],\n64:   \"reason\": \"Source search lowercases and compares only bookmark.title; the fixed target F06/A07 contract adjusts it to title, derived hostname and description, combined with the selected category. Raw URL text, category names and tags are not additional keyword fields. This clarifies target design only; accepted observations, evidence IDs, source revision and disposition remain unchanged.\"\n65:  },\n66:  {\n67:   \"capability\": \"Open a saved record as a navigation to its stored original URL, preserving the URL text and never fetching, proxying or prefetching the destination during save, listing or open preparation.\",\n68:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n69:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n70:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_93ff254508846f11\"\n71:   ],\n72:   \"reason\": \"Source opens the URL with window.open(url, '_blank', 'noopener,noreferrer') after updating visit state. The target renders the record URL as an ordinary HTTP(S) link or server redirect with the same new-tab/no-referrer intent; opening is a user navigation distinct from saving, and the Python server does not request the target page.\"\n73:  },\n74:  {\n75:   \"capability\": \"Do not enrich saved records with third-party metadata or favicon services and do not prefetch saved target pages; stored title, description and URL come from the user or local derivation.\",\n76:   \"disposition\": \"not_adopted\",\n77:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n78:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_7d47d725a2e9b759\",\n79:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_8e11efc61a4650ba\",\n80:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_ec303a2fd1afa287\"\n81:   ],\n82:   \"reason\": \"The source calls api.microlink.io and images.weserv.nl/Google s2 favicons on save and treats failures as silent. The target P0 deliberately omits these outbound calls because saving and opening must remain distinct from fetching; no target-page response, metadata or icon is retrieved, and no source enrichment behavior is presented as target design.\"\n83:  },\n84:  {\n85:   \"capability\": \"Soft-delete an active record into a recoverable trash and restore it later, instead of allowing deletion only on archived items with a transient toast undo.\",\n86:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n87:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n88:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_4c56ef30a1785be1\",\n89:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_93ef917a193a45ab\"\n90:   ],\n91:   \"reason\": \"Source facts limit Delete to archived items and provide recovery only through an Undo action on the toast, with no trash view and no deletion path for active records. The target uses an explicit soft-delete/restore lifecycle exposed in HTML so records remain recoverable; this changes the source's archived-only and transient-recovery model.\"\n92:  }\n93: ]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/application-atlas-production-pack/atlas/template-factory/jobs/job_7742b1c124be4c9ab3a0096da5cdd772/attempt-4/blueprint-code-0-1/source/CASE_DESIGN.json, lines 1-93\n1: [\n2:  {\n3:   \"capability\": \"F08: a single-user personal library persisted in SQLite that survives browser sessions and server restarts, with records queried from the database for every request rather than held in a browser store.\",\n4:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n5:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n6:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_35e41aab676021eb\",\n7:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_86ed2327f33a3ca8\",\n8:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_922f1dbc84912d99\",\n9:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_e7dd8d32c05c39f9\"\n10:   ],\n11:   \"reason\": \"The evidence shows Dexie writes on save/delete and a one-time db.bookmarks.toArray() hydration into an in-memory RippleMap, scoped to one browser profile with no sync. The target adopts local, single-user, cross-session retention but replaces IndexedDB/Dexie and in-memory hydration with SQLite on the Python server; it does not claim browser-profile persistence, multi-device sync, or the source map as target design.\"\n12:  },\n13:  {\n14:   \"capability\": \"F11: the library is delivered as server-rendered HTML pages and forms with POST/redirect/GET for add, edit and organize actions, including a ready empty-library view.\",\n15:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n16:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n17:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_06c81a165e03c96a\",\n18:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_86ed2327f33a3ca8\",\n19:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_e7dd8d32c05c39f9\"\n20:   ],\n21:   \"reason\": \"The evidence describes a client-mounted SPA: Edit is an in-page dialog populated from item fields, and component creation loads Dexie rows into a client RippleMap. The target renders lists, forms and empty state as Python 3.12 HTML responses, so the SPA mount, client-side dialog state and Dexie hydration are not carried over; only the save-now/find-later user loop is retained.\"\n22:  },\n23:  {\n24:   \"capability\": \"A deliberate save creates a URL-anchored record with a stable id, derived hostname, createdAt and initial state, and later edits preserve the record identity and creation/visit fields.\",\n25:   \"disposition\": \"adopted\",\n26:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n27:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_05babdea64ba9858\"\n28:   ],\n29:   \"reason\": \"Evidence defines bm-prefixed UUID identity, hostname derivation, createdAt and default state, and preserves id/createdAt/visit fields on edit. The target adopts this record lifecycle as a user-facing capability, with SQLite providing durability; the source's free-text tag constraints are treated separately in the category decision, not silently imported as target rules.\"\n30:  },\n31:  {\n32:   \"capability\": \"URL validation accepts only absolute, parseable HTTP(S) URLs with a nonempty valid hostname, allows single-label hosts such as http://localhost, preserves the original URL text, and rejects malformed, non-HTTP(S) or empty-host input without writing; no DNS or online-reachability check is performed.\",\n33:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n34:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n35:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_1596da4a90687ca5\"\n36:   ],\n37:   \"reason\": \"The upstream Valibot rule is a dotted-host regex that requires a dot-separated domain and an alphabetic top-level suffix, so it rejects localhost. That regex is retained as a source fact and mapped as adjusted, not reused as the target rule: the target parses the URL, checks the http/https scheme, absolute form and hostname presence, permits single-label hosts, and stores the entered string unchanged.\"\n38:  },\n39:  {\n40:   \"capability\": \"Create, rename and delete named categories with validation and with protection or reassignment when a category still contains records, assign one at save time, move records between categories, and default uncategorized saves into an Inbox category.\",\n41:   \"disposition\": \"new_design\",\n42:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n43:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_3168bcd465b6a043\",\n44:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_6bbd7a588896fe31\"\n45:   ],\n46:   \"reason\": \"Evidence shows the source has no category entity: classification is only up to five free-text tags, there is no collection CRUD or separate move, and the form rejects saves with zero tags. The target therefore designs first-class categories, an inbox default for unclassified capture and an explicit move action; these are new target concepts, not source-derived tag behavior.\"\n47:  },\n48:  {\n49:   \"capability\": \"Browse one category and see only its active records, with a category count that agrees with the listed records after adds, moves and restores.\",\n50:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n51:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n52:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_c4ad7e52e5713628\",\n53:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_9ab6b0e51811a16d\"\n54:   ],\n55:   \"reason\": \"Source facts derive tag counts by scanning all in-memory bookmarks and filter records by requiring every selected tag. The target computes category counts and category-scoped lists in SQL over active, non-deleted rows so the count and the list stay consistent; the source tag-sidebar algorithm is not the target implementation.\"\n56:  },\n57:  {\n58:   \"capability\": \"Search the selected category by keyword across title, hostname and description using case-insensitive substring matching, retaining category and query and rendering matching or explicit empty results.\",\n59:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n60:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n61:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_9ab6b0e51811a16d\",\n62:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_e62ae7e0a2c68ba1\"\n63:   ],\n64:   \"reason\": \"Source search lowercases and compares only bookmark.title; the fixed target F06/A07 contract adjusts it to title, derived hostname and description, combined with the selected category. Raw URL text, category names and tags are not additional keyword fields. This clarifies target design only; accepted observations, evidence IDs, source revision and disposition remain unchanged.\"\n65:  },\n66:  {\n67:   \"capability\": \"Open a saved record as a navigation to its stored original URL, preserving the URL text and never fetching, proxying or prefetching the destination during save, listing or open preparation.\",\n68:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n69:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n70:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_93ff254508846f11\"\n71:   ],\n72:   \"reason\": \"Source opens the URL with window.open(url, '_blank', 'noopener,noreferrer') after updating visit state. The target renders the record URL as an ordinary HTTP(S) link or server redirect with the same new-tab/no-referrer intent; opening is a user navigation distinct from saving, and the Python server does not request the target page.\"\n73:  },\n74:  {\n75:   \"capability\": \"Do not enrich saved records with third-party metadata or favicon services and do not prefetch saved target pages; stored title, description and URL come from the user or local derivation.\",\n76:   \"disposition\": \"not_adopted\",\n77:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n78:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_7d47d725a2e9b759\",\n79:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_8e11efc61a4650ba\",\n80:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_ec303a2fd1afa287\"\n81:   ],\n82:   \"reason\": \"The source calls api.microlink.io and images.weserv.nl/Google s2 favicons on save and treats failures as silent. The target P0 deliberately omits these outbound calls because saving and opening must remain distinct from fetching; no target-page response, metadata or icon is retrieved, and no source enrichment behavior is presented as target design.\"\n83:  },\n84:  {\n85:   \"capability\": \"Soft-delete an active record into a recoverable trash and restore it later, instead of allowing deletion only on archived items with a transient toast undo.\",\n86:   \"disposition\": \"adjusted\",\n87:   \"evidence_ids\": [\n88:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_4c56ef30a1785be1\",\n89:    \"ev_ba200adf6e2c_93ef917a193a45ab\"\n90:   ],\n91:   \"reason\": \"Source facts limit Delete to archived items and provide recovery only through an Undo action on the toast, with no trash view and no deletion path for active records. The target uses an explicit soft-delete/restore lifecycle exposed in HTML so records remain recoverable; this changes the source's archived-only and transient-recovery model.\"\n92:  }\n93: ]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/application-atlas-production-pack/atlas/template-factory/jobs/job_7742b1c124be4c9ab3a0096da5cdd772/attempt-4/blueprint-code-0-1/source/CASE_DESIGN.json\"}"},"time":{"start":1792433729703,"end":1792433729717}}}}
